# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un corso IBM gratuito sull'informazione e il calcolo quantistico"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products and projections"
msgstr "Prodotti interni e proiezioni"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"To better prepare ourselves to explore the capabilities and limitations of quantum circuits, we now introduce some additional mathematical concepts — namely the *inner product* between vectors (and its connection to the Euclidean norm), the notions of *orthogonality* and *orthonormality* for sets of vectors, and *projection* matrices, which will allow us to introduce a handy generalization of standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"Per prepararci meglio a esplorare le capacità e i limiti dei circuiti quantistici, introduciamo ora alcuni concetti matematici aggiuntivi: il *prodotto interno* tra vettori (e il suo legame con la norma euclidea), le nozioni di *ortogonalità* e *ortonormalità* per insiemi di vettori, e le matrici di *proiezione*, che ci permetteranno di introdurre una comoda generalizzazione delle misurazioni nella base standard.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products {#inner-products}"
msgstr "Prodotti interni {#inner-products}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that when we use the Dirac notation to refer to an arbitrary column vector as a ket, such as\n"
msgstr "Ricordiamo che quando utilizziamo la notazione di Dirac per indicare un generico vettore colonna come ket, ad esempio\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the corresponding bra vector is the *conjugate transpose* of this vector:\n"
msgstr "il corrispondente vettore bra è il *trasposto coniugato* di questo vettore:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if we have some classical state set $\\Sigma$ in mind, and we express a column vector as a ket,\n"
"such as\n"
msgstr ""
"In alternativa, se abbiamo in mente un insieme di stati classici $\\Sigma$ ed esprimiamo un vettore colonna come ket,\n"
"ad esempio\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then the corresponding row (or bra) vector is the conjugate transpose\n"
msgstr "allora il corrispondente vettore riga (o bra) è il trasposto coniugato\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that the product of a bra vector and a ket vector, viewed as matrices either having a single row or a single column, results in a scalar.\n"
"Specifically, if we have two column vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Abbiamo anche che il prodotto di un vettore bra e un vettore ket, visti come matrici con una singola riga o una singola colonna, dà come risultato uno scalare.\n"
"In particolare, se abbiamo due vettori colonna\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that the row vector $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is as in equation $(1)$, then\n"
msgstr "in modo che il vettore riga $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ sia come nell'equazione $(1)$, allora\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, if we have two column vectors that we have written as\n"
msgstr "In alternativa, se abbiamo due vettori colonna scritti come\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is the row vector $(2)$, we find that\n"
msgstr "in modo che $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ sia il vettore riga $(2)$, troviamo che\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the last equality follows from the observation that $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ and $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ for classical states $a$ and $b$ satisfying $a\\neq b$.\n"
msgstr "dove l'ultima uguaglianza segue dall'osservazione che $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ e $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ per stati classici $a$ e $b$ con $a\\neq b$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ is called the *inner product* between the vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Inner products are critically important in quantum information and computation;\n"
"we would not get far in understanding quantum information at a mathematical level without them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il valore $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ è chiamato il *prodotto interno* tra i vettori $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ e $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"I prodotti interni sono fondamentali nell'informazione e nel calcolo quantistico;\n"
"non potremmo comprendere l'informazione quantistica a livello matematico senza di essi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us now collect together some basic facts about inner products of vectors.\n"
msgstr "Raccogliamo ora alcune proprietà fondamentali dei prodotti interni tra vettori.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Relationship to the Euclidean norm.** The inner product of any vector\n"
msgstr "**Relazione con la norma euclidea.** Il prodotto interno di un qualsiasi vettore\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   with itself is\n"
msgstr "   con se stesso è\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Thus, the Euclidean norm of a vector may alternatively be expressed as\n"
msgstr "   Quindi, la norma euclidea di un vettore può essere espressa alternativamente come\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Notice that the Euclidean norm of a vector must always be a nonnegative real number.\n"
"   Moreover, the only way the Euclidean norm of a vector can be equal to zero is if every one of the entries is equal to zero, which is to say that the vector is the zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Nota che la norma euclidea di un vettore è sempre un numero reale non negativo.\n"
"   Inoltre, l'unico modo in cui la norma euclidea di un vettore può essere uguale a zero è se ogni elemento è uguale a zero, ovvero che il vettore è il vettore nullo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We can summarize these observations like this: for every vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ we have\n"
msgstr "   Possiamo riassumere queste osservazioni così: per ogni vettore $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ abbiamo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   with $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ if and only if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   This property of the inner product is sometimes referred to as _positive definiteness_.\n"
msgstr ""
"   con $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ se e solo se $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   Questa proprietà del prodotto interno viene talvolta chiamata _definitezza positiva_.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Conjugate symmetry.** For any two vectors\n"
msgstr "**Simmetria coniugata.** Per due qualsiasi vettori\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   we have\n"
msgstr "   abbiamo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   and therefore\n"
msgstr "   e quindi\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Linearity in the second argument (and conjugate linearity in the first).**\n"
"Let us suppose that $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$, $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers. If we define a new vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Linearità nel secondo argomento (e linearità coniugata nel primo).**\n"
"Supponiamo che $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ e $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ siano vettori e $\\alpha_1$ e $\\alpha_2$ siano numeri complessi. Se definiamo un nuovo vettore\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   then\n"
msgstr "   allora\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is to say, the inner product is _linear_ in the second argument.\n"
"   This can be verified either through the formulas above or simply by noting that matrix multiplication is linear in each argument (and specifically in the second argument).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Vale a dire, il prodotto interno è _lineare_ nel secondo argomento.\n"
"   Questo si può verificare sia attraverso le formule precedenti, sia semplicemente notando che la moltiplicazione matriciale è lineare in ciascun argomento (e in particolare nel secondo).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Combining this fact with conjugate symmetry reveals that the inner product is _conjugate linear_ in the first argument. That is, if $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle$, $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers, and we define\n"
msgstr "   Combinando questo fatto con la simmetria coniugata si scopre che il prodotto interno è _lineare coniugatamente_ nel primo argomento. Ovvero, se $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ e $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ sono vettori e $\\alpha_1$ e $\\alpha_2$ sono numeri complessi, e definiamo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"For every choice of vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ having the same number of entries, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"**La disuguaglianza di Cauchy–Schwarz.**\n"
"Per ogni coppia di vettori $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ e $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ con lo stesso numero di elementi, abbiamo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This is an incredibly handy inequality that gets used quite extensively in quantum information (and in many other topics of study).\n"
msgstr "   Questa è una disuguaglianza straordinariamente utile, ampiamente impiegata nell'informazione quantistica (e in molti altri ambiti di studio).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthogonal and orthonormal sets {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"
msgstr "Insiemi ortogonali e ortonormali {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are said to be *orthogonal* if their inner product is zero:\n"
msgstr "Due vettori $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ e $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ si dicono *ortogonali* se il loro prodotto interno è zero:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometrically, we can think about orthogonal vectors as vectors at right angles to each other.\n"
msgstr "Geometricamente, possiamo pensare ai vettori ortogonali come vettori perpendicolari tra loro.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthogonal set* if every vector in the set is orthogonal to every other vector in the set.\n"
"That is, this set is orthogonal if\n"
msgstr ""
"Un insieme di vettori $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ è detto *insieme ortogonale* se ogni vettore dell'insieme è ortogonale a tutti gli altri.\n"
"In altri termini, l'insieme è ortogonale se\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for which $j\\neq k$.\n"
msgstr "per ogni scelta di $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ con $j\\neq k$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthonormal* set if it is an orthogonal set and, in addition, every vector in the set is a unit vector.\n"
"Alternatively, this set is an orthonormal set if we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Un insieme di vettori $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ è detto *ortonormale* se è un insieme ortogonale e, in aggiunta, ogni vettore dell'insieme è un vettore unitario.\n"
"In alternativa, tale insieme è ortonormale se vale\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"
msgstr "per ogni scelta di $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a set $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal basis* if, in addition to being an orthonormal set, it forms a basis.\n"
"This is equivalent to $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ being an orthonormal set and $m$ being equal to the dimension of the space from which $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Infine, un insieme $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ è una *base ortonormale* se, oltre a essere un insieme ortonormale, forma una base.\n"
"Ciò equivale a richiedere che $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ sia un insieme ortonormale e che $m$ sia uguale alla dimensione dello spazio da cui $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ sono tratti.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, for any classical state set $\\Sigma$, the set of all standard basis vectors\n"
msgstr "Ad esempio, per qualsiasi insieme di stati classici $\\Sigma$, l'insieme di tutti i vettori della base standard\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is an orthonormal basis.\n"
"The set $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $2$-dimensional space corresponding to a single qubit, and the Bell basis $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $4$-dimensional space corresponding to two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"è una base ortonormale.\n"
"L'insieme $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ è una base ortonormale per lo spazio $2$-dimensionale corrispondente a un singolo qubit, e la base di Bell $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ è una base ortonormale per lo spazio $4$-dimensionale corrispondente a due qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extending orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"
msgstr "Estendere insiemi ortonormali a basi ortonormali {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are vectors that live in an $n$-dimensional space, and assume moreover that $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal set.\n"
"Orthonormal sets are always linearly independent sets, so these vectors necessarily span a subspace of dimension $m$.\n"
"From this we conclude that $m\\leq n$ because the dimension of the subspace spanned by these vectors cannot be larger than the dimension of the entire space from which they're drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Supponiamo che $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ siano vettori che vivono in uno spazio $n$-dimensionale, e supponiamo inoltre che $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ sia un insieme ortonormale.\n"
"Gli insiemi ortonormali sono sempre insiemi linearmente indipendenti, quindi questi vettori necessariamente generano un sottospazio di dimensione $m$.\n"
"Da questo concludiamo che $m\\leq n$, poiché la dimensione del sottospazio generato da questi vettori non può essere maggiore della dimensione dell'intero spazio da cui sono tratti.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it is the case that $m<n$, then it is always possible to choose an additional $n-m$ vectors\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ so that\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forms an orthonormal basis.\n"
"A procedure known as the *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* can be used to construct these vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Se $m<n$, è sempre possibile scegliere altri $n-m$ vettori\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ tali che\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ formi una base ortonormale.\n"
"Una procedura nota come *processo di ortonormalizzazione di Gram–Schmidt* può essere utilizzata per costruire questi vettori.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthonormal sets and unitary matrices {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"
msgstr "Insiemi ortonormali e matrici unitarie {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets of vectors are closely connected with unitary matrices.\n"
"One way to express this connection is to say that the following three statements are logically equivalent (meaning that they are all true or all false) for any choice of a square matrix $U$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gli insiemi ortonormali di vettori sono strettamente connessi alle matrici unitarie.\n"
"Un modo per esprimere questa connessione è affermare che le seguenti tre affermazioni sono logicamente equivalenti (cioè sono tutte vere o tutte false) per qualsiasi matrice quadrata $U$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix $U$ is unitary (that is, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr "La matrice $U$ è unitaria (ovvero $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rows of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Le righe di $U$ formano un insieme ortonormale.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The columns of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Le colonne di $U$ formano un insieme ortonormale.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equivalence is actually pretty straightforward when we think about how matrix multiplication and the conjugate transpose work.\n"
"Suppose, for instance, that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Questa equivalenza è abbastanza diretta quando pensiamo a come funzionano la moltiplicazione matriciale e il trasposto coniugato.\n"
"Supponiamo, ad esempio, di avere una matrice $3\\times 3$ come questa:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugate transpose of $U$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Il trasposto coniugato di $U$ appare così:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiplying the two matrices, with the conjugate transpose on the left-hand side, gives us this matrix:\n"
msgstr "Moltiplicando le due matrici, con il trasposto coniugato a sinistra, otteniamo questa matrice:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we form three vectors from the columns of $U$,\n"
msgstr "Se formiamo tre vettori dalle colonne di $U$,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then we can alternatively express the product above as follows:\n"
msgstr "possiamo esprimere alternativamente il prodotto precedente come segue:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to the equation $(3)$, we now see that the condition that this matrix is equal to the identity matrix is equivalent to the orthonormality of the set $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Riferendosi all'equazione $(3)$, vediamo ora che la condizione affinché questa matrice sia uguale alla matrice identità equivale all'ortonormalità dell'insieme $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This argument generalizes to unitary matrices of any size.\n"
"The fact that the rows of a matrix form an orthonormal basis if and only if the matrix is unitary then follows from the fact that a matrix is unitary if and only if its transpose is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo argomento si generalizza a matrici unitarie di qualsiasi dimensione.\n"
"Il fatto che le righe di una matrice formino una base ortonormale se e solo se la matrice è unitaria segue poi dal fatto che una matrice è unitaria se e solo se il suo trasposto è unitario.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the equivalence described above, together with the fact that every orthonormal set can be extended to form an orthonormal basis, we conclude the following useful fact:\n"
"Given any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ drawn from an $n$-dimensional space, there exists a unitary matrix $U$ whose first $m$ columns are the vectors $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Pictorially, we can always find a unitary matrix having this form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Data l'equivalenza descritta sopra, insieme al fatto che ogni insieme ortonormale può essere esteso per formare una base ortonormale, concludiamo il seguente fatto utile:\n"
"Dato qualsiasi insieme ortonormale di vettori $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ tratti da uno spazio $n$-dimensionale, esiste una matrice unitaria $U$ le cui prime $m$ colonne sono i vettori $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Graficamente, possiamo sempre trovare una matrice unitaria di questa forma:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the last $n-m$ columns are filled in with any choice of vectors $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ that make\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ an orthonormal basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qui, le ultime $n-m$ colonne vengono completate con una qualsiasi scelta di vettori $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ che rendono\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ una base ortonormale.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projections and projective measurements {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Proiezioni e misurazioni proiettive {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projection matrices {#projection-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrici di proiezione {#projection-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A square matrix $\\Pi$ is called a *projection* if it satisfies two properties:\n"
msgstr "Una matrice quadrata $\\Pi$ è detta *proiezione* se soddisfa due proprietà:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices that satisfy the first condition — that they are equal to their own conjugate transpose — are called *Hermitian matrices*, and matrices that satisfy the second condition — that squaring them leaves them unchanged — are called *idempotent* matrices.\n"
msgstr "Le matrici che soddisfano la prima condizione — ovvero che sono uguali alla propria trasposta coniugata — sono chiamate *matrici Hermitiane*, mentre quelle che soddisfano la seconda condizione — elevandole al quadrato rimangono invariate — sono chiamate matrici *idempotenti*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a word of caution, the word *projection* is sometimes used to refer to any matrix that satisfies just the second condition but not necessarily the first, and when this is done the term *orthogonal projection* is typically used to refer to matrices satisfying both properties.\n"
"In the context of quantum information and computation, however, the terms *projection* and *projection matrix* more typically refer to matrices satisfying both conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"È opportuno fare una precisazione: il termine *proiezione* viene talvolta usato per indicare qualsiasi matrice che soddisfa solo la seconda condizione, non necessariamente la prima; in tal caso si usa il termine *proiezione ortogonale* per le matrici che soddisfano entrambe le proprietà.\n"
"Nel contesto dell'informazione e del calcolo quantistico, tuttavia, i termini *proiezione* e *matrice di proiezione* si riferiscono più comunemente alle matrici che soddisfano entrambe le condizioni.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An example of a projection is the matrix\n"
msgstr "Un esempio di proiezione è la matrice\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any unit vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"We can see that this matrix is Hermitian as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"per qualsiasi vettore unitario $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Possiamo verificare che questa matrice è Hermitiana nel modo seguente:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, to obtain the second equality, we have used the formula\n"
msgstr "Qui, per ottenere la seconda uguaglianza, abbiamo usato la formula\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is always true, for any two matrices $A$ and $B$ for which the product $AB$ makes sense.\n"
msgstr "che è sempre valida per qualsiasi coppia di matrici $A$ e $B$ per cui il prodotto $AB$ abbia senso.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see that the matrix $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ is idempotent, we can use the assumption that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a unit vector, so that it satisfies $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Thus, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Per verificare che la matrice $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ è idempotente, usiamo l'ipotesi che $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ sia un vettore unitario, e quindi soddisfi $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Abbiamo quindi\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, if $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is any orthonormal set of vectors, then the matrix\n"
msgstr "Più in generale, se $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ è un qualsiasi insieme ortonormale di vettori, allora la matrice\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a projection.\n"
"Specifically, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"è una proiezione.\n"
"In particolare, abbiamo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "e\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the orthonormality of $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implies the second-to-last equality.\n"
msgstr "dove l'ortonormalità di $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implica la penultima uguaglianza.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this exhausts all of the possibilities: *every* projection $\\Pi$ can be written in the form $(5)$ for some choice of an orthonormal set $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Technically speaking, the zero matrix $\\Pi=0$, which is a projection, is a special case.\n"
"To fit it into the general form $(5)$ we must allow the possibility that the sum is empty, resulting in the zero matrix.)\n"
msgstr ""
"In realtà, questo esaurisce tutte le possibilità: *ogni* proiezione $\\Pi$ può essere scritta nella forma $(5)$ per una qualche scelta di un insieme ortonormale $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Tecnicamente, la matrice zero $\\Pi=0$, che è una proiezione, costituisce un caso particolare.\n"
"Per inserirla nella forma generale $(5)$ è necessario ammettere la possibilità di una somma vuota, che dà appunto la matrice zero.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Misurazioni proiettive {#projective-measurements}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a measurement of a quantum system is more general than just standard basis measurements.\n"
"*Projective measurements* are measurements that are described by a collection of projections whose sum is equal to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols, a collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ of projection matrices describes a projective measurement if\n"
msgstr ""
"Il concetto di misurazione di un sistema quantistico è più generale delle semplici misurazioni nella base standard.\n"
"Le *misurazioni proiettive* sono misurazioni descritte da una collezione di proiezioni la cui somma è uguale alla matrice identità.\n"
"In simboli, una collezione $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ di matrici di proiezione descrive una misurazione proiettiva se\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it is in some state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, two things happen:\n"
msgstr "Quando tale misurazione viene eseguita su un sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ che si trova in uno stato $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, accadono due cose:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, the outcome of the measurement is $k$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Per ogni $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, il risultato della misurazione è $k$ con probabilità uguale a\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{il risultato è $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $k$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Per qualunque risultato $k$ produca la misurazione, lo stato di $\\mathsf{X}$ diventa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also choose outcomes other than $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ for projective measurements if we wish.\n"
"More generally, for any finite and nonempty set $\\Sigma$, if we have a collection of projection matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"È possibile scegliere anche risultati diversi da $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ per le misurazioni proiettive.\n"
"Più in generale, per qualsiasi insieme finito e non vuoto $\\Sigma$, se abbiamo una collezione di matrici di proiezione\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that satisfies the condition\n"
msgstr "che soddisfa la condizione\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then this collection describes a projective measurement whose possible outcomes coincide with the set $\\Sigma$, where the rules are the same as before:\n"
msgstr "allora questa collezione descrive una misurazione proiettiva i cui possibili risultati coincidono con l'insieme $\\Sigma$, dove le regole sono le stesse di prima:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $a\\in\\Sigma$, the outcome of the measurement is $a$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Per ogni $a\\in\\Sigma$, il risultato della misurazione è $a$ con probabilità uguale a\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{il risultato è $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $a$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Per qualunque risultato $a$ produca la misurazione, lo stato di $\\mathsf{X}$ diventa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, standard basis measurements are equivalent to projective measurements, where $\\Sigma$ is the set of classical states of whatever system $\\mathsf{X}$ we're talking about and our set of projection matrices is\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le misurazioni nella base standard sono ad esempio equivalenti a misurazioni proiettive, dove $\\Sigma$ è l'insieme degli stati classici del sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ in questione e l'insieme delle matrici di proiezione è\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another example of a projective measurement, this time on two qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, is given by the set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, where\n"
msgstr ""
"Un altro esempio di misurazione proiettiva, questa volta su due qubit $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, è dato dall'insieme\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, dove\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we have multiple systems that are jointly in some quantum state and a projective measurement is performed on just one of the systems, the action is similar to what we had for standard basis measurements — and in fact we can now describe this action in much simpler terms than we could before.\n"
msgstr "Se abbiamo più sistemi che si trovano congiuntamente in uno stato quantistico e si esegue una misurazione proiettiva su uno solo di essi, l'effetto è analogo a quello che abbiamo visto per le misurazioni nella base standard — e di fatto ora possiamo descrivere questa azione in termini molto più semplici rispetto a prima.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, let us suppose that we have two systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, and a projective measurement described by a collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ is performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$, while nothing is done to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Doing this is then equivalent to performing the projective measurement described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Per essere precisi, supponiamo di avere due sistemi $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in uno stato quantistico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, e che una misurazione proiettiva descritta dalla collezione $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ venga eseguita sul sistema $\\mathsf{X}$, mentre non viene fatto nulla su $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Questo è equivalente a eseguire la misurazione proiettiva descritta dalla collezione\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Each measurement outcome $a$ results with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"sul sistema congiunto $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Ogni risultato di misurazione $a$ si ottiene con probabilità\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and conditioned on the result $a$ appearing, the state of the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "e condizionatamente all'esito $a,$ lo stato del sistema congiunto $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ diventa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementing projective measurements {#implementing-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Implementare le misurazioni proiettive {#implementing-projective-measurements}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arbitrary projective measurements can be implemented using unitary operations, standard basis measurements, and an extra workspace system, as will now be explained.\n"
msgstr "Le misurazioni proiettive arbitrarie possono essere implementate tramite operazioni unitarie, misurazioni nella base standard e un sistema di lavoro aggiuntivo, come verrà spiegato di seguito.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system and $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$. We can easily generalize this discussion to projective measurements having different sets of outcomes, but in the interest of convenience and simplicity we will assume the set of possible outcomes for our measurement is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Supponiamo che $\\mathsf{X}$ sia un sistema e $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ una misurazione proiettiva su $\\mathsf{X}$. Potremmo facilmente generalizzare questa discussione a misurazioni proiettive con diversi insiemi di risultati, ma per semplicità assumeremo che l'insieme dei possibili risultati sia $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us note explicitly that $m$ is not necessarily equal to the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ — we'll let $n$ be the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, which means that each matrix $\\Pi_k$ is an $n\\times n$ projection matrix.\n"
msgstr "Notiamo esplicitamente che $m$ non è necessariamente uguale al numero di stati classici di $\\mathsf{X}$ — indicheremo con $n$ il numero di stati classici di $\\mathsf{X}$, il che significa che ogni matrice $\\Pi_k$ è una matrice di proiezione $n\\times n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we assume that $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ represents a projective measurement, it is necessarily the case that\n"
msgstr "Poiché assumiamo che $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ rappresenti una misurazione proiettiva, è necessariamente vero che\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to perform a process that has the same effect as performing this projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$, but to do this using only unitary operations and standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr "Il nostro obiettivo è eseguire un processo che abbia lo stesso effetto dell'esecuzione di questa misurazione proiettiva su $\\mathsf{X}$, ma utilizzando solo operazioni unitarie e misurazioni nella base standard.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will make use of an extra workspace system $\\mathsf{Y}$ to do this, and specifically we'll take the classical state set of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, which is the same as the set of outcomes of the projective measurement.\n"
"The idea is that we will perform a standard basis measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, and interpret the outcome of this measurement as being equivalent to the outcome of the projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We'll need to assume that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to some fixed state, which we'll choose to be $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Any other choice of fixed quantum state vector could be made to work, but choosing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ makes the explanation to follow much simpler.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Per farlo utilizzeremo un sistema di lavoro aggiuntivo $\\mathsf{Y}$, e in particolare sceglieremo come insieme di stati classici di $\\mathsf{Y}$ l'insieme $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, che coincide con l'insieme dei risultati della misurazione proiettiva.\n"
"L'idea è di eseguire una misurazione nella base standard su $\\mathsf{Y}$ e interpretarne il risultato come equivalente al risultato della misurazione proiettiva su $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Dovremo assumere che $\\mathsf{Y}$ sia inizializzato in uno stato fisso, che scegliamo essere $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Qualsiasi altra scelta di vettore di stato quantistico fisso funzionerebbe, ma scegliere $\\vert 0\\rangle$ rende molto più semplice la spiegazione che segue.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, in order for a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to tell us anything about $\\mathsf{X}$, we will need to allow $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ to interact somehow before measuring $\\mathsf{Y}$, by performing a unitary operation on the system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"First consider this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ovviamente, affinché una misurazione nella base standard di $\\mathsf{Y}$ ci dica qualcosa su $\\mathsf{X}$, dovremo permettere che $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ interagiscano in qualche modo prima di misurare $\\mathsf{Y}$, eseguendo un'operazione unitaria sul sistema $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"Consideriamo prima questa matrice:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed explicitly as a so-called *block matrix*, which is essentially a matrix of matrices that we interpret as a single, larger matrix, $M$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Espressa esplicitamente come una cosiddetta *matrice a blocchi* — ovvero una matrice di matrici che interpretiamo come un'unica matrice di dimensioni maggiori — $M$ si presenta così:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, each $0$ represents an $n\\times n$ matrix filled entirely with zeros, so that the entire matrix $M$ is an $nm\\times nm$ matrix.\n"
msgstr "Qui, ogni $0$ rappresenta una matrice $n\\times n$ interamente composta di zeri, cosicché l'intera matrice $M$ è una matrice $nm\\times nm.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, $M$ is certainly not a unitary matrix (unless $m=1$, in which case $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I}$, giving $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in this trivial case) because unitary matrices cannot have any columns (or rows) that are entirely $0$; unitary matrices have columns that form orthonormal bases, and the all-zero vector is not a unit vector.\n"
msgstr "Ora, $M$ non è certamente una matrice unitaria (a meno che $m=1,$ nel qual caso $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ il che dà $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in questo caso banale) perché le matrici unitarie non possono avere colonne (o righe) interamente pari a $0;$ le matrici unitarie hanno colonne che formano basi ortonormali, e il vettore tutto-zero non è un vettore unitario.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is the case that the first $n$ columns of $M$ are orthonormal, and we get this from the assumption that $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a measurement.\n"
"To verify this claim, notice that for each $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, the vector formed by column number $j$ of $M$ is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tuttavia, le prime $n$ colonne della matrice $M$ sono ortonormali, e questo segue dall'ipotesi che $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ sia una misurazione.\n"
"Per verificare questa affermazione, si noti che per ogni $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, il vettore formato dalla colonna numero $j$ di $M$ è il seguente:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that here we're numbering the columns starting from column $0$. Taking the inner product of column $i$ with column $j$ when $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ gives\n"
msgstr "Nota che qui stiamo numerando le colonne a partire dalla colonna $0$. Calcolando il prodotto interno della colonna $i$ con la colonna $j$ per $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ si ottiene\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what we needed to show.\n"
msgstr "che è esattamente ciò che volevamo dimostrare.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, because the first $n$ columns of the matrix $M$ are orthonormal, we can replace all of the remaining zero entries by some different choice of complex number entries so that the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr "Quindi, poiché le prime $n$ colonne della matrice $M$ sono ortonormali, possiamo sostituire tutte le voci zero rimanenti con valori complessi opportuni in modo che l'intera matrice sia unitaria.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we're given the matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, we can compute suitable matrices to fill in for the blocks marked $\\fbox{?}$ in the equation — using the Gram–Schmidt process — but it does not matter specifically what these matrices are for the sake of this discussion.\n"
msgstr "Date le matrici $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, possiamo calcolare le matrici adatte da inserire al posto dei blocchi contrassegnati con $\\fbox{?}$ — tramite il processo di Gram–Schmidt — ma per questa discussione non è importante sapere esattamente quali siano.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we can describe the measurement process: we first perform $U$ on the joint system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Y}$ with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"For an arbitrary state $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ of $\\mathsf{X}$, we obtain the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Possiamo infine descrivere il processo di misurazione: prima eseguiamo $U$ sul sistema congiunto $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ e poi misuriamo $\\mathsf{Y}$ con una misurazione nella base standard.\n"
"Per un arbitrario stato $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ di $\\mathsf{X}$, otteniamo lo stato\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first equality follows from the fact that $U$ and $M$ agree on their first $n$ columns.\n"
"When we perform a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, we obtain each outcome $k$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"dove la prima uguaglianza segue dal fatto che $U$ e $M$ coincidono sulle prime $n$ colonne.\n"
"Quando eseguiamo una misurazione nella base standard su $\\mathsf{Y}$, otteniamo ciascun risultato $k$ con probabilità\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "nel qual caso lo stato di $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ diventa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stores a copy of the measurement outcome and $\\mathsf{X}$ changes precisely as it would had the projective measurement described by $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ been performed directly on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "Quindi, $\\mathsf{Y}$ memorizza una copia del risultato della misurazione e $\\mathsf{X}$ cambia esattamente come farebbe se la misurazione proiettiva descritta da $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ fosse stata eseguita direttamente su $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
